swept away in this feeling of, I must do more, and stay grounded more in decency, kindness, and true compassion, concern for humanity. And that in turn will affect their own well-being. Absolutely. There are more and more studies now saying if you are good and compassionate and kind, that this helps your own well-being. Altruism helps you feel better about yourself. There are studies showing psychological well-being is better. They're physiological studies that show this. So yes, doing for others makes you feel good.

11
